WEBVTT

00:04.590 --> 00:05.580
Hello.

00:05.580 --> 00:07.900
This is Fujiwara no
Teika, out on a stroll.

00:07.900 --> 00:12.310
I'm on Mount Ogura, which
hosts the villa where I live.

00:12.310 --> 00:13.740
Teika-kun!

00:14.960 --> 00:16.740
Wait for me!

00:17.310 --> 00:19.630
This is Utsunomiya Yoritsuna.

00:19.630 --> 00:22.870
A relative who lives in a
villa on this mountain.

00:23.330 --> 00:24.960
You see, the Hyakunin Isshu was

00:24.960 --> 00:28.130
compiled to decorate the
screens in his villa.

00:28.130 --> 00:28.750
Right?

00:28.750 --> 00:30.170
Huh?  Y-Yes...

00:31.050 --> 00:33.160
I thought that screens
decorated by poems

00:33.160 --> 00:35.130
would make the place look more chic,

00:35.130 --> 00:39.180
so I decided on one poem from each
poet for a total of one hundred poems.

00:39.730 --> 00:42.350
And I chose the poems.

00:42.620 --> 00:46.030
Anyway, I'm glad to see you
doing better, Teika-kun.

00:46.030 --> 00:46.560
Huh?

00:46.560 --> 00:52.030
1235: Emperor Go-Horikawa commissions
Fujiwara no Teika to compile the

00:46.560 --> 00:52.030
Shin
Chokusen Wakashu

00:47.320 --> 00:50.890
Your Shin Chokusen Wakashu was such a flop,

00:50.890 --> 00:52.030
you got all sulky.

00:52.530 --> 00:54.680
It was painful to watch.

00:55.790 --> 00:57.990
It wasn't my fault...

00:57.990 --> 01:02.730
The big wigs kept changing stuff around!

01:03.140 --> 01:04.500
I-I know!

01:04.500 --> 01:06.310
That's why I wanted to give you a chance

01:06.310 --> 01:08.780
to truly express yourself
with this private anthology!

01:10.500 --> 01:12.050
Yoritsuna-kun...

01:14.570 --> 01:15.560
Love ya.

02:47.220 --> 02:49.430
Hello again.  This is Teika.

02:49.430 --> 02:50.720
Sorry to spring this on you,

02:50.720 --> 02:53.490
but which Hyakunin Isshu
poet is the first one

02:53.490 --> 02:55.230
that comes to mind?

02:55.250 --> 02:57.550
Emperor Tenji, Emperor Jito, Kakinomoto no Hitomaro,

02:55.950 --> 02:58.960
Many of these poets are
known for other works

02:57.550 --> 03:00.250
Yamabe no Akahito, Sarumaru Dayu, Councilor Yakamochi,

02:58.960 --> 03:01.350
of literature and poetry,
which made them famous.

03:00.250 --> 03:02.550
Abe no Nakamaro, The Monk Kisen, Ono no Komachi, Semimaru,

03:01.350 --> 03:04.280
The Hyakunin Isshu includes
poems from all kinds of poets.

03:02.550 --> 03:05.250
Advisor Takamura, The Monk Henjo, The Former Emperor Yozei,

03:05.200 --> 03:07.200
For example, there is the
Former Emperor Yozei,

03:05.250 --> 03:07.200
Minister of the Left of Kawara, Emperor Koko, Councilor Yukihira

03:07.750 --> 03:10.600
who happens to be the son of Takaiko
from the previous episode.

03:10.600 --> 03:12.280
His name is Sadaakira.

03:12.680 --> 03:16.460
The Hyakunin Isshu includes his
only poem that is still on record.

03:17.230 --> 03:18.630
Selected by me.

03:19.840 --> 03:29.220
Prince
Sadaakira

03:19.840 --> 03:29.220
Emperor Yozei (Age 9)

03:19.840 --> 03:29.220
The
Former
Emperor
Yozei
(Age 17)

03:20.460 --> 03:23.250
Sadaakira became emperor
at the young age of nine,

03:23.250 --> 03:25.520
before abdicating at the
slightly less young age of seventeen

03:25.520 --> 03:27.570
and becoming the Former Emperor Yozei.

03:27.570 --> 03:29.880
While he was Emperor,
he was served by

03:29.880 --> 03:33.490
Ariwa no Narihira, the man who
almost eloped with Takaiko.

03:34.650 --> 03:39.530
The rumors say that
Sadaakira was quite wild...

03:41.240 --> 03:43.460
M-My Lord, please stop!

03:49.250 --> 03:50.040
What is the matter?

03:50.040 --> 03:51.500
Oh, my lady!

03:51.500 --> 03:52.830
Hey, Yasuko!

03:53.860 --> 03:56.140
Isn't this a nice horse?

03:56.920 --> 03:59.670
Though it's a little feisty.

04:05.790 --> 04:07.800
Hello, Sadaakira-sama.

04:08.240 --> 04:10.060
Would you care to join
me for some refreshment?

04:10.730 --> 04:11.950
What?

04:11.950 --> 04:14.520
You must be tired after the hard ride.

04:15.690 --> 04:18.570
She's always smiling like a fool...

04:19.720 --> 04:21.970
Even when I first met her.

04:22.780 --> 04:26.780
Sadaakira and Yasuko

04:22.780 --> 04:26.780
The Former Emperor Yozei

04:30.710 --> 04:31.660
Hey, wait up!

04:42.300 --> 04:44.320
Is something the matter, My Lady?

04:44.890 --> 04:46.810
Oh, General.

04:46.810 --> 04:48.430
It's nothing for you to worry about.

04:55.760 --> 04:57.400
Here, My Lady.

04:58.230 --> 04:59.440
It's fixed.

05:00.080 --> 05:02.230
Wow, thank you!

05:15.300 --> 05:20.580
My Lord, I told you to stop
playing kemari indoors.

05:20.580 --> 05:21.300
Who was that?

05:21.670 --> 05:22.600
Excuse me?

05:22.600 --> 05:24.550
That girl with the stupid smile.

05:25.010 --> 05:27.260
Oh, you mean Minamoto no Yasuko-sama.

05:28.360 --> 05:30.800
She serves as a playmate
for your younger sister,

05:31.380 --> 05:33.770
and visits the palace from time to time.

05:35.570 --> 05:37.730
Wouldn't you agree that
she's a very lovely girl?

05:37.730 --> 05:39.940
H-How is she lovely?!

05:39.940 --> 05:41.290
She's ugly!  Butt ugly!

05:42.670 --> 05:44.220
After that...

05:45.040 --> 05:46.390
Mother!

05:47.750 --> 05:49.370
Oh, Sadaakira.

05:49.370 --> 05:51.120
Are you going to join us?

05:54.360 --> 05:55.500
No way!

06:03.800 --> 06:06.050
H-Hello, Sadaakira-sama.

06:06.820 --> 06:08.450
G-Go away!

06:16.160 --> 06:17.330
My Lord?

06:25.750 --> 06:26.780
I'm mad.

06:27.390 --> 06:28.670
She makes me mad!

06:28.670 --> 06:30.560
She needs to be punished!

06:30.560 --> 06:32.090
In that case, My Lord,

06:32.090 --> 06:33.530
let us study poetry.

06:34.200 --> 06:36.670
Huh?  Why poetry?

06:36.670 --> 06:39.490
I want to punish her.

06:40.030 --> 06:41.820
My Lord, poetry is...

06:41.820 --> 06:45.480
I hate poetry!

06:45.480 --> 06:46.980
Good grief...

06:46.980 --> 06:48.840
I guess that's it for today, then.

06:49.130 --> 06:50.980
W-Wait!  A story!

06:50.980 --> 06:53.280
I'll let you tell me a story
about one of your trips!

06:55.140 --> 06:58.340
Then I'll tell you about when
I traveled to the Eastern lands.

06:59.860 --> 07:02.380
I ended up on Mount Tsukuba.

07:02.380 --> 07:04.210
The mountain has two peaks.

07:04.210 --> 07:05.680
The west peak is known as Mount Male.

07:05.680 --> 07:07.680
The east peak is known as Mount Female.

07:07.680 --> 07:09.450
Oh, that's crazy.

07:10.200 --> 07:11.250
Is this how it looks?

07:11.250 --> 07:14.240
No, they look like normal peaks.

07:14.570 --> 07:16.460
Oh, that's boring.

07:16.460 --> 07:18.670
No, it's actually quite interesting.

07:18.670 --> 07:22.120
A festival is held on this mountain.

07:22.120 --> 07:22.960
Festival?

07:24.020 --> 07:27.300
It is a village ritual
where many people gather

07:27.300 --> 07:30.510
to dance, sing, and freely enjoy life.

07:31.290 --> 07:33.190
It is the only day when the

07:33.190 --> 07:35.350
mountain gods allow the people to

07:35.350 --> 07:37.920
forget everything else and seek free love.

07:40.090 --> 07:43.770
There is a stream which
begins on the two peaks

07:43.770 --> 07:46.380
and joins with other streams

07:46.380 --> 07:48.940
before becoming a river
that flows out to sea.

07:49.010 --> 07:55.330
Like young romance maturing
into passionate love.

07:56.950 --> 08:00.680
You always make everything about love.

08:00.680 --> 08:02.230
That wasn't interesting at all.

08:03.600 --> 08:05.500
You will understand
soon enough, My Lord.

08:05.500 --> 08:08.420
What's that mean?
You're making me mad.

08:26.690 --> 08:27.860
It's so noisy...

08:28.180 --> 08:31.170
Man, the frogs are so loud.

08:31.170 --> 08:33.150
I can't get any sleep.

08:35.380 --> 08:36.440
That's...

08:38.210 --> 08:39.090
Hey.

08:41.360 --> 08:43.260
Good evening, Sadaakira-sama.

08:43.260 --> 08:45.550
Why are you here?

08:46.160 --> 08:48.630
I was playing with your younger sister.

08:49.100 --> 08:52.520
But it got so late that I was
told to stay here tonight.

08:53.470 --> 08:56.010
You think you're a
palace court lady now?

08:58.160 --> 08:59.040
No...

08:59.470 --> 09:02.220
Sitting out here by yourself...

09:02.220 --> 09:05.270
A monster will eat you up!

09:05.270 --> 09:06.440
O-Oh...

09:07.300 --> 09:08.600
What?

09:09.390 --> 09:11.520
Your reactions are so dull.

09:12.090 --> 09:15.890
The palace will look bad if
there's a fool like you around.

09:15.890 --> 09:17.910
You better leave in the morning.

09:18.370 --> 09:19.390
Yes.

09:19.390 --> 09:21.250
So what are you doing?

09:21.700 --> 09:22.460
What?

09:23.010 --> 09:25.870
Why are you out here by yourself?

09:28.670 --> 09:32.630
I liked the sound of the frogs,
so I wanted to listen from up close.

09:33.060 --> 09:34.100
Huh?

09:36.140 --> 09:38.370
They're just making a bunch of noise.

09:38.370 --> 09:39.860
You believe that they're noisy?

09:40.630 --> 09:43.840
Could you please forgive them?

09:45.590 --> 09:48.590
Frogs don't live as long as humans.

09:48.590 --> 09:51.020
They're singing with all
they have right now.

09:51.990 --> 09:55.030
In the summer, I like to
listen to the cicadas.

09:56.030 --> 09:57.810
When I think about how these

09:57.810 --> 10:00.530
small creatures are
doing the best they can,

10:01.920 --> 10:05.000
it makes me want to try harder.

10:13.640 --> 10:15.880
Good night, Sadaakira-sama.

10:21.180 --> 10:22.990
How to get rid of the frogs?

10:22.990 --> 10:24.010
Yeah, give me an answer!

10:26.620 --> 10:28.190
Yes...

10:28.190 --> 10:30.280
You could try using snakes.

10:30.280 --> 10:31.100
Snakes?

10:31.100 --> 10:33.360
Yes, because snakes eat frogs.

10:33.960 --> 10:36.190
How do they eat frogs when
they don't have hands?

10:36.190 --> 10:37.900
They swallow them whole.

10:37.900 --> 10:38.570
Swallow them whole?

10:39.280 --> 10:43.870
Yes, and the snake looks quite
funny with its bloated stomach.

10:44.270 --> 10:46.290
Ooh, that sounds fun.

10:47.130 --> 10:48.720
Thanks, General!

10:49.380 --> 10:51.570
I'm glad that I could help.

10:55.880 --> 10:56.540
What?!

10:56.540 --> 10:57.300
What's wrong?!

10:57.300 --> 10:58.750
Sna-Sna—

10:58.750 --> 10:59.730
Snakes!

10:59.730 --> 11:01.200
Whoa, what's this?!

11:01.200 --> 11:02.800
Where did they all come from?!

11:03.200 --> 11:05.530
Quick!  Chase them away!

11:05.530 --> 11:07.050
How do we do that?!

11:07.050 --> 11:08.940
Should we use a net to capture them?!

11:10.490 --> 11:12.350
No!  No!  Stay away!

11:13.390 --> 11:15.300
Why are you running away?

11:15.300 --> 11:17.520
You should be helping the frogs!

11:17.900 --> 11:21.950
Look, your little friends
are being gobbled up!

11:22.610 --> 11:24.800
They're crying because they
can no longer sing!

11:24.800 --> 11:25.850
Shouldn't you save them?

11:25.850 --> 11:29.330
Come on, didn't you say you
were going to try harder?

11:29.330 --> 11:32.580
You should stop smiling like a fool
if you're going to be useless.

11:33.160 --> 11:34.740
That's enough, My Lord!

11:34.740 --> 11:36.220
You'll lose her regard.

11:36.220 --> 11:37.970
Huh?  So what?

11:37.970 --> 11:39.860
I don't care what she thinks about me...

11:39.860 --> 11:40.730
...you.

11:41.770 --> 11:42.680
I hate you!

11:43.220 --> 11:45.350
I hate you, Sadaakira-sama!

11:47.030 --> 11:48.560
See, I told you so.

11:49.830 --> 11:51.480
S-Same here...

11:52.220 --> 11:54.140
I hate your guts!

11:54.910 --> 11:57.350
Serves you right, ugly!  Ugly!  Ugly!

11:57.350 --> 11:58.400
Butt ugly!

12:02.100 --> 12:03.160
Honestly...

12:03.740 --> 12:05.360
I wouldn't have told you about the snakes,

12:05.360 --> 12:07.220
if I'd known you would pull such a prank.

12:07.220 --> 12:09.780
Shut up.  I was punishing her.

12:09.780 --> 12:12.370
It was difficult to clean up your mess.

12:12.980 --> 12:14.620
I couldn't care less.

12:14.620 --> 12:18.090
Everybody thinks I'm a hassle anyway.

12:19.840 --> 12:22.210
Nobody feels that way about you.

12:22.210 --> 12:23.050
Don't lie.

12:23.910 --> 12:26.110
I can tell.

12:26.110 --> 12:28.610
It didn't matter who became Emperor.

12:28.610 --> 12:31.980
They chose me, a kid, so
they could have free rein.

12:33.010 --> 12:35.230
So I'll also do as I please.

12:35.710 --> 12:39.230
That's what they get for looking
down on me because I'm a kid.

12:39.830 --> 12:41.240
Okay, General.

12:41.240 --> 12:42.610
Teach me how to use a sword.

12:42.610 --> 12:44.210
That looks fun.

12:44.600 --> 12:47.920
In that case, you will need
to study poetry instead

12:47.920 --> 12:50.000
of listening to stories about my travels.

12:50.000 --> 12:50.790
Huh?

12:51.280 --> 12:53.480
Are you stupid, General?

12:53.480 --> 12:54.810
I want to learn about
swords, not poetry.

12:54.810 --> 12:56.570
Are you going deaf?

12:56.570 --> 12:58.100
No, My Lord.

12:58.100 --> 13:01.420
A mischievous boy like you
needs to learn poetry.

13:01.910 --> 13:03.960
I'm not mischievous!

13:03.960 --> 13:05.020
Poems are boring!

13:05.540 --> 13:07.300
Please wait, My Lord.

13:07.850 --> 13:10.650
Nobody knows how long
I will be able to serve you.

13:10.930 --> 13:13.060
What?  Are you going to quit?

13:13.510 --> 13:18.300
No, I intend to serve you
until you ask me to quit.

13:18.910 --> 13:20.690
I'll never do that!

13:20.690 --> 13:21.480
But...

13:22.870 --> 13:26.240
I do not know if I will
live to see you grow up,

13:26.730 --> 13:30.700
so I wish to teach you what
I can while I'm still here.

13:31.920 --> 13:33.850
Please have a seat.

13:37.910 --> 13:39.170
Poetry is wonderful.

13:40.060 --> 13:43.840
You're allowed to freely
express your feelings,

13:45.020 --> 13:47.710
because it's an escape route.

13:47.710 --> 13:48.740
Escape route?

13:48.740 --> 13:49.510
Yes.

13:49.510 --> 13:55.640
Je t'aime

13:50.390 --> 13:53.640
For example, let's pretend
that you're using

13:53.640 --> 13:55.600
some mushy talk to win over a girl.

13:55.920 --> 13:57.530
If she turns you down,

13:57.530 --> 13:59.820
it's a crushing blow that will
leave you with nothing

13:59.820 --> 14:01.120
but humiliation and grief.

14:01.120 --> 14:03.180
But, if you express your
feelings in a poem,

14:03.180 --> 14:05.990
you can use the excuse
that it was just a poem.

14:06.350 --> 14:08.750
Isn't that just putting up a tough front?

14:08.750 --> 14:10.370
If the poem is written well enough,

14:10.370 --> 14:11.820
it will be passed down
to future generations.

14:11.820 --> 14:13.070
A nice bonus.

14:13.070 --> 14:14.660
And a little contemptible.

14:15.530 --> 14:17.640
It sounds like poetry is a joke.

14:17.640 --> 14:19.230
That was a waste of time.

14:19.230 --> 14:21.210
That is what makes poetry so good.

14:22.520 --> 14:24.330
Because poetry isn't taken seriously,

14:24.330 --> 14:27.620
you're able to say things you
normally wouldn't be able to.

14:28.420 --> 14:29.840
When reciting a poem,

14:29.840 --> 14:33.880
you release your own bonds,
freeing yourself to be honest.

14:34.970 --> 14:37.960
Well?  Isn't that perfect
for a mischievous boy?

14:37.960 --> 14:40.310
I'm not mischievous.

14:42.800 --> 14:48.480
Less than a year later,
Narihira passed away.

14:55.020 --> 14:56.450
Mother!

14:57.200 --> 14:58.400
Mother!

15:00.170 --> 15:01.530
What's wrong?

15:02.460 --> 15:05.980
It's nothing.
I was just reminiscing.

15:07.190 --> 15:08.670
What about you?

15:09.760 --> 15:11.840
Why do you look so sad?

15:12.890 --> 15:14.260
The General...

15:15.080 --> 15:17.390
Narihira died!

15:21.020 --> 15:21.850
Yes...

15:23.230 --> 15:24.830
It will be sad without him around.

15:26.290 --> 15:29.500
I really liked him.

15:31.380 --> 15:34.190
Narihira was the only person

15:34.190 --> 15:36.700
besides my mother who
truly cared about me

15:36.700 --> 15:40.290
and understood me.

15:41.240 --> 15:44.960
After his death, I got along
even worse with everyone else.

15:47.240 --> 15:49.130
M-My Lord, please stop!

15:49.130 --> 15:50.840
Shut up!  Get lost!

15:51.750 --> 15:53.670
That was when my mother's older brother,

15:53.670 --> 15:57.310
Chancellor of the realm Fujiwara
no Mototsune, made his decision.

15:58.360 --> 16:01.940
At age 17, my reign came to an end.

16:01.350 --> 16:03.230
Prince Tokiyasu

16:01.940 --> 16:04.070
Prince Tokiyasu was named Emperor.

16:03.230 --> 16:05.860
Emperor Koko

16:05.050 --> 16:07.270
His son, Minamoto no Sadami,

16:06.880 --> 16:08.610
Minamoto no Sadami

16:07.270 --> 16:09.560
was named Crown Prince,

16:08.610 --> 16:10.280
Prince Sadami

16:09.560 --> 16:10.880
and would later succeed him.

16:10.280 --> 16:12.530
Emperor Uda

16:11.560 --> 16:14.060
In order to avoid any conflict
between Sadami and myself,

16:14.060 --> 16:17.990
the court had Sadami's younger
sister wedded to me.

16:18.940 --> 16:20.540
Sadami's younger sister

16:20.540 --> 16:23.000
was Yasuko.

16:24.080 --> 16:25.450
Poor Yasuko.

16:25.450 --> 16:27.620
For her brother, for her country,

16:27.620 --> 16:30.450
she was forced to give
herself to a man she hated.

16:31.730 --> 16:33.710
Pitiful.

16:33.710 --> 16:36.930
How does it feel to be
wedded to a man you hate,

16:37.300 --> 16:39.030
worthless frog girl?

16:42.020 --> 16:44.080
You remembered me.

16:45.610 --> 16:48.140
I tried as hard as I could.

16:48.860 --> 16:51.490
I look forward to spending the
rest of our lives together.

16:53.180 --> 16:56.370
Her words still only anger me.

17:00.310 --> 17:01.770
Sadaakira-sama,

17:01.770 --> 17:03.790
the moon is beautiful tonight.

17:05.240 --> 17:07.460
Thank you for visiting me tonight.

17:07.870 --> 17:10.580
I'm only here because
there's someone who

17:10.580 --> 17:11.880
gets on my case if I don't visit.

17:11.880 --> 17:12.760
I'm going to sleep.

17:13.320 --> 17:15.070
You must be tired.

17:15.070 --> 17:18.780
Allow me to prepare the bed
so you can get some rest.

17:21.890 --> 17:24.520
Yasuko, you should find
yourself a lover.

17:24.910 --> 17:25.540
What?

17:26.270 --> 17:27.870
Or do you already have one?

17:28.480 --> 17:31.190
You're always smiling like a fool
without a care in the world,

17:31.750 --> 17:34.530
so you must have someone to comfort you.

17:35.770 --> 17:37.200
What do you mean?

17:37.610 --> 17:39.370
I'm being considerate.

17:40.140 --> 17:43.810
It would be sad,
if you were with a brute like me

17:43.810 --> 17:45.240
for the rest of your life.

17:45.590 --> 17:48.380
I'm sure you're starting to feel
frustrated that I won't touch you.

17:48.950 --> 17:50.900
Go find some other man to satisfy you.

17:50.900 --> 17:52.330
I don't mind.

17:53.280 --> 17:57.510
I'm sure that she's heard
many nasty stories about me.

17:58.570 --> 18:01.180
When a pawn cannot be
controlled, he's cut loose.

18:01.180 --> 18:04.630
It's easy to take away a
young emperor's reign.

18:05.300 --> 18:08.350
But none of them ever
tried to understand me.

18:09.000 --> 18:11.500
You're the same as the
rest of them, Yasuko.

18:14.390 --> 18:17.610
I never expected you to
suggest I be unfaithful.

18:18.750 --> 18:23.250
What?  I'm thinking of your future.

18:23.250 --> 18:25.580
I didn't marry you for love.

18:26.440 --> 18:28.880
I'm sure the same goes for you, right?

18:28.880 --> 18:30.260
This is what everybody else does.

18:30.260 --> 18:31.540
You're free to do as you please.

18:33.200 --> 18:34.930
That does not make it

18:34.930 --> 18:37.510
acceptable for me to behave improperly.

18:39.240 --> 18:40.510
But as a woman,

18:40.510 --> 18:42.590
you want to experience
love eventually, right?

18:42.590 --> 18:43.250
Yes...

18:45.290 --> 18:46.430
with you.

18:48.940 --> 18:50.650
Aren't you supposed to hate me?

18:51.150 --> 18:53.120
Yes, I do not like you,

18:53.720 --> 18:56.770
but we are husband and wife now.

18:56.770 --> 18:58.860
I am prepared to fall in love with you.

18:59.900 --> 19:02.300
I would be hiding from the truth if

19:02.300 --> 19:05.350
I were to be unfaithful because
of an unwanted marriage.

19:06.560 --> 19:08.870
I will not escape from the
partner I've been given.

19:09.480 --> 19:12.290
I will try my best to
fall in love with him.

19:13.880 --> 19:15.670
What are you trying to accomplish?

19:15.670 --> 19:18.520
You seem to enjoy testing
people, Sadaakira-sama.

19:18.520 --> 19:19.400
I find it unpleasant!

19:20.070 --> 19:20.880
Hey!

19:20.880 --> 19:22.020
I realize it's difficult for you

19:22.020 --> 19:24.150
to trust anyone after everything
you've been through,

19:24.150 --> 19:26.080
but you shouldn't become a coward.

19:26.080 --> 19:27.010
Coward?!

19:27.810 --> 19:29.870
Listen to me, Sadaakira-sama.

19:30.390 --> 19:32.560
I will never betray you.

19:33.870 --> 19:37.440
Remember this well.

19:44.060 --> 19:45.680
Please be careful.

19:45.680 --> 19:47.330
I hope that you visit me again.

19:57.300 --> 20:00.600
You're able to say things you
normally wouldn't be able to.

20:01.090 --> 20:02.630
When reciting a poem,

20:02.630 --> 20:06.730
you release your own bonds,
freeing yourself to be honest.

20:09.350 --> 20:10.660
Bring the ink.

20:11.080 --> 20:12.220
I must write a letter.

20:14.020 --> 20:15.480
Feel love deepen over time,

20:15.480 --> 20:19.720
like the stream widening into a river

20:19.720 --> 20:21.400
as it descends Mount Tsukuba.

20:23.900 --> 20:26.320
The uncertain feelings I once had

20:26.320 --> 20:28.250
have grown over time,

20:28.900 --> 20:30.020
and now

20:30.940 --> 20:32.540
you are very dear to me.

20:33.740 --> 20:34.820
My Lady?

20:37.400 --> 20:39.830
My Lady, what is the matter?

20:39.830 --> 20:43.230
Did he say something mean again?

20:43.230 --> 20:44.000
No...

20:44.720 --> 20:47.390
I was just surprised
because he was able to

20:48.550 --> 20:50.280
speak his mind.

20:55.660 --> 20:57.470
Wh-What are you doing?!

20:57.470 --> 20:58.570
Are you crazy?!

20:59.340 --> 21:02.450
Thank you for sending me the
lovely poem this morning.

21:03.310 --> 21:04.570
I was very happy.

21:04.950 --> 21:06.750
Th-That was...

21:06.750 --> 21:08.310
That was just a courtesy!

21:08.310 --> 21:09.730
Don't take it seriously, ugly!

21:09.730 --> 21:11.260
You're lying.

21:11.260 --> 21:13.900
I understand how you truly feel now.

21:13.900 --> 21:15.710
You don't!  You don't understand me!

21:16.290 --> 21:20.440
Yes, we have plenty of time
to understand one another.

21:29.410 --> 21:33.360
The story of the fall of
the Former Emperor Yozei

21:33.040 --> 21:43.480
Sandai
Jitsuroku

21:33.040 --> 21:43.480
Compiled by Fujiwara no Tokihira
and Sugawara no Michizane in 901

21:33.360 --> 21:37.140
is recorded in the Sandai Jitsuroku.

21:37.140 --> 21:39.690
Many history books use
this text as a basis

21:39.690 --> 21:42.540
for labeling the Former
Emperor Yozei as a tyrant.

21:43.480 --> 21:54.950
Feel love deepen over time, like the stream
widening into a river as it descends Mount Tsukuba.

21:44.420 --> 21:48.160
However, the poem he wrote has been

21:48.160 --> 21:51.390
interpreted as an expression of a love

21:51.390 --> 21:53.450
he didn't realize he felt.

21:55.480 --> 21:57.210
Emperor Yozei the tyrant.

21:57.950 --> 21:59.500
Emperor Yozei the poet.

21:59.520 --> 22:12.970
The Former

21:59.520 --> 22:12.970
Emperor Yozei

22:00.340 --> 22:03.320
Unfortunately, we will never know

22:03.320 --> 22:06.400
which was the true Yozei,

22:06.400 --> 22:09.220
but we would have known much less,

22:09.220 --> 22:12.970
if he had never written
down his love for Yasuko.

22:13.480 --> 22:16.610
A single poem of love was able

22:16.610 --> 22:18.940
to carry a message across time.

22:19.420 --> 22:22.980
It's possible that one of
your messages to a loved one

22:22.980 --> 22:25.720
will reach someone in the distant future.

22:26.410 --> 22:30.840
How will your poem of love be
interpreted in the future?

22:32.930 --> 22:34.910
Poetic Tale 2:

22:32.930 --> 22:34.910
END

24:04.980 --> 24:19.910
Next Episode

24:04.980 --> 24:19.910
Munesada and Yoshiko

24:04.980 --> 24:19.910
The Monk Henjo

24:06.840 --> 24:11.200
The sky is the road home
for the holy maidens;

24:11.830 --> 24:18.210
may the wind bring clouds
to extend their stay.
